  geometry: l1d_sets=128, l1d_ways=8, l2_sets=1024, l2_ways=8, llc_sets=1024, llc_ways=8
    because: The LLC has extremely low hit rates across all workloads and its misses overwhelmingly go to memory; shrinking it to the minimum allowed size removes 6 cycles of hit latency from the critical path of these misses.
  replacement: l2_replacement=ship, llc_replacement=ship
    because: Since SHiP improved LLC performance, applying it to the L2 cache might similarly improve retention of useful lines amidst prefetch pollution.
  concurrency: l2_mshr=64, llc_mshr=64
    because: Since 128 LLC MSHRs performed worse than 32 but 32 might be slightly restrictive given the high miss rate on W1, testing 64 LLC MSHRs can find the optimal concurrency balance.

