Prefetch mechanisms and the levels that accept each:
  no             L1D, L2C, LLC  no prefetching.
  next_line      L1D, L2C, LLC  fetches the line after the one accessed; no training and no history, so it is always timely and is right only where access is sequential.
  ip_stride      L1D, L2C, LLC  learns a constant stride per load instruction and runs ahead of it; needs a few repeats of the same instruction to train, covers regular strides only.
  va_ampm_lite   L1D, L2C       keeps an access map of the lines touched in each page and prefetches the lines whose offset pattern already appeared in the map; needs the page's history to accumulate, covers irregular but spatially clustered access.
  spp_dev        L2C, LLC       compresses the recent deltas within a page into a signature, predicts the next delta from it and follows the path several lines ahead; the deepest and most aggressive, and the one that needs the longest history and the most misses to learn from.
Capacity and the hit latency it costs (latency follows capacity alone):
  L1D: 16 KB 3 cy | 24 KB 3 cy | 32 KB 4 cy | 48 KB 4 cy | 64 KB 4 cy | 96 KB 5 cy
  L2C: 64 KB 4 cy | 128 KB 6 cy | 256 KB 7 cy | 512 KB 9 cy | 1024 KB 12 cy | 2048 KB 15 cy
  LLC: 512 KB 9 cy | 1024 KB 12 cy | 2048 KB 15 cy | 4096 KB 19 cy | 8192 KB 24 cy

